# Spec 026 — Norway on the LiveNear Map

Status: Draft
Owner: <you>
Related: GitHub #14; 007 (coverage and repo size), 011/013/016 (commute),
014/020 (affordability, payment budget), 019 (matches), 025 (routes),
`docs/livenear/sources.md` (terms log)

## Overview

Add Norway to LiveNear: home prices and commute reach on the same map, in
kroner and metric units. Coverage is every kommune with published data, and
Oslo is split into delbydeler so the capital can answer commute questions at
a useful scale.

## Context

The map is US-only, but regions, geofence and colour ramps are already
data-driven. The obstacles are a US-only geocoder, 5-digit join keys, a
required `median_value`, and US assumptions in formatting and mortgage
defaults. Free Norwegian prices are published as average NOK/m², not as a
median home value, which is the main modelling change. The owner has accepted
Oslo's statistics bank on the strength of its open-data listing (see the terms
log). Repo data is 114.9 MB against a ~120 MB limit (007 R2).

## Requirements

### Data

- **R1 — Sources.** Prices come from SSB 14545/14310 for kommuner and Oslo
  BOL018 for delbydeler; income from SSB 06944; boundaries from Geonorge
  kommuner and grunnkretser, joined into delbydeler with SSB's KLASS 460 code
  list. Only sources with a row in the terms log are used, and listing sites
  are never touched.
- **R2 — Regions.** Norway appears as regions in the existing picker: each
  fylke, with kommune polygons, except a combined "Oslo & Akershus" region
  with Oslo as delbydeler and Akershus as kommuner, so commuters see both
  sides of the city line.
- **R3 — Sparse areas.** An area with fewer than 10 sales in the period, or no
  published price, has no value and renders as no-data. It is never imputed.
- **R4 — Oslo is removable.** Oslo delbydel data is one separable build
  output. Without it, Oslo falls back to one SSB kommune polygon.
- **R5 — Size.** Norway adds at most 5 MB to committed data, or the 007 limit
  is explicitly revised in this spec first.
- **R6 — Build.** A separate `build_data_norway.py` produces the committed
  files, reprojects from EPSG:25833 to WGS84 and is unit-tested. The US
  pipeline is unchanged.

### Model

- **R7 — Region descriptor.** Each region declares its country, currency,
  timezone, units, area-type wording and available metrics. Absent fields mean
  US defaults, so existing data files keep working.
- **R8 — Area IDs.** Area keys are opaque strings. Norwegian 4-digit kommune
  codes keep their leading zeros and 8-digit codes survive; US ZIP handling is
  unchanged.
- **R9 — Price metric.** Norwegian areas carry price per m², labelled as an
  average. The estimated home price used for budget matching is price per m²
  times a reference home size, shown beside the result and adjustable by the
  user. The default is 75 m², marked as an estimate.
- **R10 — Metric availability.** A metric a region lacks is hidden. The picker
  never offers an empty layer. Sold $/sqft is hidden for Norway.
- **R11 — Trend.** Change-over-time figures never span the 2024/2025 boundary,
  where SSB's m² definition changed.

### Commute

- **R12 — Geocoding.** Address search accepts Norwegian addresses, and results
  outside covered regions are still refused.
- **R13 — Time.** Norwegian regions use `Europe/Oslo` all year, so departure
  times are never in the past, with rush windows set for Norway per region
  rather than the US 16:30-18:00.
- **R14 — Ferries.** Routes may use ferries, as today, and the commute note
  says so for Norwegian regions.

### Presentation

- **R15 — Formatting.** Norwegian regions show kr, m², km² and km, and 24-hour
  time. Wording says Fylke and Kommune or Delbydel, not State or ZIP. The
  landing page's LiveNear coverage line includes Norway.
- **R16 — URLs.** Shared links with Norwegian region and area IDs round-trip.
  A budget applies only in its own currency: changing country clears it, and
  a link carrying a budget and a Norwegian region reads it as kroner.
- **R17 — Mortgage defaults.** Norwegian payment-mode defaults are marked as
  estimates with a written basis: 10% minimum equity, and a note that banks
  also cap debt at 5x income and test a 3-point rate rise (minimum 7%).
  Payment mode states that it does not check those limits.
- **R18 — Affordability.** Price-to-income appears only where a matching income
  figure exists. Oslo delbydeler use their bydel's income, labelled as a bydel
  figure wherever it is shown. Matches fall back to price per m² ranking where
  no income exists.
- **R19 — Attribution.** About lists SSB, the City of Oslo and Kartverket with
  the credit their licences require, and flags that SSB figures were adapted.

## Non-functional / Constraints

- Norway adds no new API key, database or personal data.
- Mapbox calls stay inside the existing daily budget and county-level
  geofences (one all-Norway box would also admit most of Sweden).

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Every Norwegian region loads with shaded areas; Oslo shows delbydeler
      (R2).
- [ ] Areas under 10 sales render as no-data (R3); removing the Oslo output
      leaves a working single-polygon Oslo (R4).
- [ ] Committed Norway data is within budget (R5), and US data and tests are
      unchanged (R6, R7).
- [ ] Code `0301` and an 8-digit code both survive load and URL round-trips
      (R8, R16).
- [ ] A budget matches on price per m² times the visible reference size (R9).
- [ ] Unavailable metrics are absent from the picker (R10); no trend spans
      2024/2025 (R11).
- [ ] An Oslo address resolves, and a Stockholm address is refused (R12).
- [ ] A commute in July uses a future Oslo departure (R13).
- [ ] Live Oslo isochrones and commutes return traffic-aware results, recorded
      in the verification notes (R13).
- [ ] Norwegian regions show kr, m², km, 24-hour time and local wording (R15).
- [ ] A US budget does not carry into Norway (R16).
- [ ] Mortgage and attribution text is present (R17, R19).
- [ ] `npm run test`, `npm run build`, `pytest`, `ruff check .` pass.

## Open Questions (resolve in review)

None open.

Resolved by the owner: 75 m² default, adjustable (R9); bydel income labelled
(R18); live Mapbox calls in Oslo approved. Resolved in the build: delbydeler
can't be derived from grunnkrets codes, but SSB's KLASS 460 maps them under
CC BY 4.0, so Oslo's unlicensed code list isn't needed.

## Out of Scope (explicit)

- Transit commutes (suggest a separate issue).
- Sub-kommune prices outside Oslo; no public source was found.
- Countries other than the US and Norway, and Norwegian-language UI.
- A bank-grade check of how much someone could borrow.

## Verification notes

R1, R3-R6 → build tests and a size check; R7-R11, R15-R18 → unit tests plus a
visual check on two fylker and Oslo at desktop and phone widths; R12-R14 →
a small number of live Mapbox calls, approved by the owner beforehand; R19 →
visual. The human verifies; the implementing agent does not self-certify done.

Live Mapbox results, 2026-11-10 (21 calls, see the terms log): Oslo isochrone
variation returned (peak 92 vs off-peak 229 sq mi); Asker-Oslo S commutes
varied with departure time; Horten-Moss used a ferry step. Geocoding resolved
Oslo and Bergen addresses. "Sveavagen 1, Stockholm" first matched a Michigan
place under `country=us,no`, then a similarly named Oslo street at relevance
0.55, so searches now use the bias region's country and drop matches below
0.6 relevance.
